    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d349">

                <pb facs="0516" n="436" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg436"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.114 Mexico/407</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Daniels</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 3238</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-01-24">January 24,
                        1936</date>.<lb/>[Received January 29.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the Embassy’s despatch
                    No. 3146 of December 23, 1935<anchor n="48" xml:id="d349-f1"/> on the above
                    mentioned subject, to previous correspondence regarding this matter, and to the
                    Department’s strictly confidential instruction No. 973 of January 6,
                        1936,<anchor n="48" xml:id="d349-f2"/> I have the honor to report to the
                    Department that I had a conversation with Licenciado Eduardo Suárez, Minister of
                    Hacienda, this morning. Licenciado Suárez informed me that he had a decree on
                    his desk which provides that shipments of alcohol out of Mexico must carry a
                    bond for the production of a landing certificate. He stated that the decree
                    would be presented to the President on Monday, January 27, and would be
                    promulgated in the <hi rendition="#italic">Diario Oficial</hi> shortly
                    thereafter. It is believed that this action will be of material assistance in
                    curbing the exportation <pb facs="0517" n="437" xml:id="pg437"/> to the United
                    States of illegal liquor shipments and will act as a deterrent in the use of
                    Mexican territory for this purpose.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Josephus Daniels</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
